{"name":"Spicy Sweetcorn","hex":"#f6ac00","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spicy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, pertaining to, or containing spice.","Of a flavor, provoking a burning sensation due to the presence of capsaicin or a similar chemical."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spicy"},{"term":"sweetcorn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of sweet corn."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweetcorn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pungency","blocks":[{"text":"Pungency, commonly referred to as spiciness, hotness or heat, is a sensation that contributes to the flavor of certain foods such as chili peppers. Highly pungent foods may be experienced as unpleasant. The term piquancy is sometimes applied to foods with a lower degree of pungency that are \"agreeably stimulating to the palate\". In addition to chili peppers, piquant ingredients include wasabi, horseradish and mustard. The primary substances responsible for pungency are capsaicin, piperine and allyl isothiocyanate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/PepperswithscovilleCentralMarketHoustonTX.JPG/330px-PepperswithscovilleCentralMarketHoustonTX.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pungency"},{"title":"Sweet corn","blocks":[{"text":"Sweet corn, also called sweetcorn, sugar corn, pole corn, or simply corn is a variety of corn (maize) grown for human consumption with a relatively high sugar content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/VegCorn.jpg/330px-VegCorn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_corn"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Epice_marche_Pointe_a_Pitre.JPG/500px-Epice_marche_Pointe_a_Pitre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u